# REST API standards

JSON over HTTP. Base path `/api/v1`. UTF-8. Resource IDs are UUIDs. Align payloads with `spec/api-contract.md`.

## Resource naming

- Plural nouns, lowercase. Multi-word path segments: kebab-case (`/api/v1/ticket-comments` only if it is its own resource).
- Nest only when the child cannot exist without the parent: `/api/v1/tickets/{ticketId}/comments`.
- No verbs in paths. Actions that are state changes are `POST` to a sub-resource: `POST /api/v1/tickets/{id}/assign`, not `/changeStatus`.
- Query params for filters/sort: `status`, `assigneeId`, `sort` (`field,asc|desc`). No camelCase in query keys — use camelCase in JSON bodies only.

| Method | Path | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/api/v1/tickets` | List (paginated) |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/tickets/{id}` | Fetch one |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/tickets` | Create |
| `PATCH` | `/api/v1/tickets/{id}` | Partial update of mutable fields |
| `DELETE` | `/api/v1/tickets/{id}` | Delete (or 405 if tickets are not deleted) |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/tickets/{id}/...` | Lifecycle action (`assign`, `resolve`, `close`) |

Prefer `PATCH` over `PUT`. Do not use `GET` for mutations.

## HTTP status codes

| Status | When |
|---|---|
| `200 OK` | Successful `GET` / `PATCH` / action that returns a body |
| `201 Created` | Successful `POST` create. Set `Location: /api/v1/tickets/{id}` |
| `204 No Content` | Successful `DELETE` with no body |
| `400 Bad Request` | Malformed JSON, wrong types, missing required JSON fields (bean validation) |
| `401 Unauthorized` | Missing/invalid credentials |
| `403 Forbidden` | Authenticated but not allowed |
| `404 Not Found` | Resource id does not exist |
| `409 Conflict` | Duplicate create, stale version, concurrent update |
| `422 Unprocessable Entity` | Syntactically valid body that violates domain/state-machine rules |
| `500 Internal Server Error` | Unexpected failures only — never as a stand-in for 4xx |

Do not return `200` with an error payload. Illegal ticket transitions are **`422`**, not `400` or `500`.

## Error body

Every 4xx/5xx uses the same shape from `GlobalExceptionHandler`. No Spring default `/error` HTML or `timestamp`/`path`-only bodies.

```json
{
  "code": "TICKET_NOT_FOUND",
  "message": "Ticket 3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6 not found",
  "details": [
    { "field": "status", "message": "must not be blank" }
  ]
}
```

- `code`: `ErrorCode` enum name (`SCREAMING_SNAKE`). Stable for clients; do not reuse codes for different meanings.
- `message`: human-readable, no stack traces, no SQL.
- `details`: optional array; empty or omitted when there are no field errors. Bean validation maps each constraint to `{ field, message }`.
- Do not wrap successes in `{ "data": ..., "success": true }`. Success body **is** the resource DTO.

## Pagination

List endpoints are paginated. Never return an unbounded array.

Query: `page` (0-based, default `0`), `size` (default `20`, max `100`), `sort` (optional).

```json
{
  "content": [ { } ],
  "page": 0,
  "size": 20,
  "totalElements": 134,
  "totalPages": 7
}
```

Map from Spring `Page<T>`. Reject `size > 100` with `400`. Empty lists are `200` with `content: []`, not `404`.
